description:
## Why

Per PKIX-amgn.8 decisions (2026-05-11): pkix-lint-cabf parses vendored OSCAL Catalog JSON via serde_json into a lean Rust struct (NOT 1:1 OSCAL mirror), tailored to what Lint impls actually look up. Consistent with Arch 2 / PKIX-9vnx.10 Risk parser pattern.

## What

In pkix-lint-cabf/src/catalog.rs (new module):

```rust
#[derive(Debug, Clone, serde::Deserialize)]
pub struct VendoredCatalog {
    /// Indexed lookup by Control ID.
    controls: BTreeMap<String, Control>,
    /// Catalog title from OSCAL metadata.
    title: String,
    /// zlint SHA this catalog was derived from.
    zlint_sha: String,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, serde::Deserialize)]
pub struct Control {
    pub id: String,
    pub title: String,
    pub statement: String,            // from parts[name=statement].prose
    pub citation: String,             // from links[rel=cites]
    pub br_section: Option<String>,   // from props[name=br-section]
    pub source_classification: String, // from props[name=source-classification]
    pub effective_date: Option<String>, // from props[name=effective-date], RFC 3339
}

impl VendoredCatalog {
    pub fn parse(json: &str) -> Result<Self, CatalogParseError>;
    pub fn get(&self, control_id: &str) -> Option<&Control>;
    pub fn iter(&self) -> impl Iterator<Item = (&String, &Control)>;
    pub fn zlint_sha(&self) -> &str;
}
```

The Deserialize impl walks OSCAL Catalog shape (catalog -> groups[]/controls[] -> control{id, title, parts[], links[], props[]}) into the lean indexed form. May be hand-written or use a serde adapter — implementation choice.

### Bake-in pattern

```rust
const CABF_BR_TLS_JSON: &str = include_str!("../catalogs/cabf-br-tls-derived-from-zlint-<sha7>.oscal.json");

pub fn cabf_br_tls() -> &'static VendoredCatalog {
    static CATALOG: OnceLock<VendoredCatalog> = OnceLock::new();
    CATALOG.get_or_init(|| VendoredCatalog::parse(CABF_BR_TLS_JSON).expect("vendored catalog must parse"))
}
```

The catalog filename embedding the zlint SHA means each refresh requires updating the include_str! path. That's a feature, not a bug — explicit version coupling.

### Error type

CatalogParseError covers: malformed JSON, missing required fields (statement, citation, source-classification), unknown OSCAL version, etc. Use thiserror.

## Acceptance

- [ ] catalog.rs module with VendoredCatalog + Control + CatalogParseError.
- [ ] include_str! + OnceLock pattern for cabf_br_tls() works.
- [ ] Unit test: parse a sample OSCAL Catalog JSON fixture (small, hand-crafted), verify get() returns expected Controls.
- [ ] Unit test: malformed JSON returns CatalogParseError, not panic.
- [ ] cabf_br_tls() called at runtime parses the vendored catalog without error (smoke test against the catalog from PKIX-amgn.8.4).

## Out of scope

- Lint impls (PKIX-amgn.8.6 demonstrates the pattern).
- Startup-invariant check (lint-id-must-match-catalog) — folded into .8.6 or follow-up.

## Depends on

PKIX-amgn.8.4 (the vendored catalog file must exist to include_str! against; can stub for unit tests but smoke needs the real file).

## Filed by

Decomposed from PKIX-amgn.8 per Mark's 2026-05-11 decisions.
